    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35746" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pervŏlĭto</span></b> ,
			āre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq. n.</i> [pervolo], <i>to
				fly through</i> or <i>around</i>, <i>to flit about</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per dissepta domorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 952</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 346</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnia loca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tecta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 4, 505</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iter,</span>”
				<i>to traverse repeatedly</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					9, 1, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
